@startuml
!theme vibrant
scale 1200 width

concise "CPU" as CPU
concise "PWM Wrap IRQ" as PWM_IRQ
concise "Timer Alarm" as ALARM
concise "ADC" as ADC
concise "DMA" as DMA
concise "DMA IRQ" as DMA_IRQ
robust "PWM Counter" as PWM_CNT
digital "Internal PWM (A)" as PWM_INT
digital "External PWM (A)" as PWM_EXT


@0
CPU is "Active"
note right of CPU: <font size=12><b>Initialization Phase</b></font>\n1. `hal_motor_init_pwm()` is called.\n   - GPIOs are configured.\n   - PWM clock divider and wrap value calculated.\n   - PWM slices are configured and enabled.\n2. `hal_motor_init_bemf_adc_dma()` is called.\n   - ADC & GPIOs are initialized.\n   - DMA channel is claimed and configured.\n   - DMA & PWM IRQ handlers are installed.
PWM_CNT is "0"
PWM_INT is 0
PWM_EXT is 1

@20
CPU is "Idle"
note right of CPU: System is idle, waiting for commands.

@40
CPU is "Active"
note right of CPU: `hal_motor_set_pwm(179)` is called\n(duty_cycle = 70%)\n`on_level` is calculated for 70% duty.\nPWM channel A level is set.

@50
CPU is "Idle"

== Operational Phase: 1x 20kHz Cycle (50µs), 70% Duty Cycle ==

@60
PWM_CNT is "0"
PWM_IRQ is "Active"
CPU is "Active"
note right of PWM_IRQ: PWM counter reaches 0,\ntriggers Wrap Interrupt.
note right of CPU: `on_pwm_wrap()` ISR begins.\n- IRQ is cleared.\n- Schedules BEMF ADC trigger\n  via hardware timer.

@62
PWM_IRQ is "Idle"
CPU is "Idle"

@65
ALARM is "Active"
note right of ALARM: Timer fires after `adc_trigger_delay_us`\n(e.g., ~5µs into the OFF phase).\nThe BEMF measurement must happen\nduring the PWM OFF period.
CPU is "Active"
note right of CPU: `delayed_adc_trigger_callback()`\n- Calls `trigger_adc_measurement()`

@66
ALARM is "Idle"
ADC is "Active"
note right of ADC: ADC is enabled and starts\nfree-running sampling.
CPU is "Active"
note right of CPU: `trigger_adc_measurement()`\n- Sets up ADC round-robin.\n- Drains ADC FIFO.\n- Re-arms DMA channel.\n- Starts ADC (`adc_run(true)`).

@67
CPU is "Idle"
DMA is "Transferring"
note right of DMA #lightblue: For every sample in the ADC FIFO,\nthe ADC peripheral asserts the DREQ signal.\nThe DMA controller responds instantly,\ntransferring one `uint16_t` sample from\nADC FIFO to the Ring Buffer in RAM.\nThis happens `BEMF_RING_BUFFER_SIZE` times.
ADC -> DMA : DREQ
@68
ADC -> DMA : DREQ
@69
ADC -> DMA : DREQ
@70
ADC -> DMA : DREQ

@75
DMA is "Idle"
ADC is "Idle"
DMA_IRQ is "Active"
note right of DMA_IRQ: DMA completes its transfer count,\ntriggers DMA Interrupt.

@76
CPU is "Active"
note right of CPU: `dma_irq_handler()` ISR begins.\n- Stops ADC (`adc_run(false)`).\n- Clears DMA IRQ flag.\n- Processes BEMF buffer.\n- Calls user callback.

@78
DMA_IRQ is "Idle"
CPU is "Idle"


/' --- Corrected PWM Waveforms for one 50µs Phase-Correct Cycle (70% Duty) ---
   1. PWM Counter (`PWM_CNT`) forms a triangle wave (0 -> TOP -> 0).
   2. `hal_motor_set_pwm` maps 70% duty to a LOW compare level (`on_level` approx. 30% of TOP).
   3. Internal PWM is HIGH when Counter < `on_level` (at start and end of cycle).
   4. External PWM is INVERSE of internal, creating a single, centered HIGH pulse.
   5. Active time: @67.5 to @102.5 = 35µs. Total cycle: 50µs. (35/50 = 70%).
'/

@60
PWM_CNT is "0"
PWM_INT is 1
PWM_EXT is 0

@67.5 /' 15% into cycle (7.5µs), counter rises above compare level. '/
PWM_CNT is "500"
PWM_INT is 0
PWM_EXT is 1

@85 /' 50% into cycle (25µs), counter reaches the peak (TOP). '/
PWM_CNT is "1000"

@102.5 /' 85% into cycle (42.5µs), counter falls below compare level. '/
PWM_CNT is "500"
PWM_INT is 1
PWM_EXT is 0

@110 /' 100% into cycle (50µs), counter is back at 0. '/
PWM_CNT is "0"
PWM_INT is 1
PWM_EXT is 0

@enduml
